{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Claim form money preview (add-claims design decision 1), the same rules as packages/core/src/claims/money.ts and the web form's apps/web/src/routes/_app/claims/-lib/money.ts. Amounts are integers in the currency's minor units (ISO 4217 exponent), rates are S$ per 1 unit as millionths, and each line is converted once, rounded half-up to the cent. The server recomputes every line; the apps only show the same S$ amount while the person types.",
  "rules": [
    "sgdCents = roundHalfUp(amountMinor × rateMicros × 100 / (10^exponent × 10^6)), computed exactly (no floating point).",
    "A rate is a positive decimal with at most 6 decimal places (no exponent, no comma). Anything else is not a rate.",
    "An amount is a positive number with at most `exponent` decimal places; commas are thousands separators and are ignored.",
    "An SGD line's S$ amount is its amount. A foreign line has no S$ amount until both the amount and the rate are valid.",
    "The claim total is the sum of the rounded line amounts."
  ],
